  "notes": "Cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative attributes the event to a procedural/knowledge gap regarding RCS pressure control with only 'A' RCP in service, but no official cause code was assigned. Two check valves per CLA (V) described only as design context (isolation function during normal operation, not implicated in the failure) and were omitted as separate component nodes per rule 6/7 guidance; ECCS subsystem trains (centrifugal charging pump, RHR pump/HX) mentioned only in Safety Analysis as design-basis credit, not modeled as System/Component nodes since they were not actually challenged or used during the event. No previous similar occurrence reported (explicitly stated none in past three years), so no SIMILAR_TO edge or stub LER emitted."
